---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<Layout
	title="Introduction to Arithmetic Progressions | Class 10 Mathematics | The Concepts Adda"
	description="Learn what an Arithmetic Progression (AP) is, first term (a), common difference (d), and identifying AP sequences according to latest NCERT."
>
	<main class="lesson-page">
		<div class="lesson-container">
			<a href="/arithmetic-progressions" class="back-link">
				<span class="back-arrow">←</span>
				<span>Back to Arithmetic Progressions</span>
			</a>

			<!-- LESSON HEADER -->
			<section class="lesson-header">
				<div class="lesson-number">01</div>
				<div class="lesson-header-copy">
					<div class="lesson-label">LESSON 01 · CLASS 10 MATHEMATICS (NCERT)</div>
					<h1>Introduction to <span>Arithmetic Progressions</span></h1>
					<p>
						Understand number sequences, first term (a), common difference (d), general form of an AP, and finite vs infinite APs.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- CONTENT LAYOUT -->
			<section class="content-layout">
				<article class="lesson-content">

					<!-- 01 · DEFINITION -->
					<div class="topic-label">01 · THE BASICS</div>
					<h2>What is an Arithmetic Progression (AP)?</h2>
					<p>
						An <strong>Arithmetic Progression (AP)</strong> is a list of numbers in which each term is obtained by adding a fixed number <em>d</em> to the preceding term except the first term <em>a</em>.
					</p>

					<div class="formula-box">
						<strong>General Form of an AP: a, a + d, a + 2d, a + 3d, ...</strong>
					</div>

					<div class="idea-box">
						<div class="idea-icon">💡</div>
						<div class="idea-content">
							<strong>Common Difference (d)</strong>
							<p>
								The fixed number <strong>d</strong> is called the <strong>common difference</strong>.
								<br/>
								<strong>d = a<sub>k</sub> - a<sub>k-1</sub></strong> &nbsp;(It can be positive, negative, or zero!).
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 02 · EXAMPLES OF APs -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">02 · EXAMPLES</div>
					<h2>Examples of AP Sequences</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Positive d</span>
							<div>
								<p><strong>1, 4, 7, 10, 13...</strong></p>
								<span style="color:#64748b; font-size:14px;">First term <em>a = 1</em>, Common difference <em>d = +3</em></span>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Negative d</span>
							<div>
								<p><strong>100, 70, 40, 10, -20...</strong></p>
								<span style="color:#64748b; font-size:14px;">First term <em>a = 100</em>, Common difference <em>d = -30</em></span>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Zero d</span>
							<div>
								<p><strong>3, 3, 3, 3, 3...</strong></p>
								<span style="color:#64748b; font-size:14px;">First term <em>a = 3</em>, Common difference <em>d = 0</em></span>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 03 · SOLVED NCERT EXAMPLE -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">03 · SOLVED EXAMPLE</div>
					<h2>Checking if a Sequence is an AP</h2>

					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 1</span>
							<h3>Which of the following forms an AP? (i) 2, 4, 8, 16... (ii) 2, 5/2, 3, 7/2...</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p><strong>(i) For 2, 4, 8, 16...</strong>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								a₂ - a₁ = 4 - 2 = 2<br/>
								a₃ - a₂ = 8 - 4 = 4
							</div>
							<p style="margin-top:10px;">Since a₂ - a₁ ≠ a₃ - a₂, the common difference is not constant. <strong>Not an AP!</strong></p>

							<p style="margin-top:16px;"><strong>(ii) For 2, 5/2, 3, 7/2...</strong>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								a₂ - a₁ = 5/2 - 2 = 1/2<br/>
								a₃ - a₂ = 3 - 5/2 = 1/2<br/>
								a₄ - a₃ = 7/2 - 3 = 1/2
							</div>
							<p style="margin-top:10px;">Since a<sub>k+1</sub> - a<sub>k</sub> is constant (1/2), <strong>this is an AP with a = 2, d = 1/2</strong>.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 04 · QUICK SUMMARY -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">04 · QUICK SUMMARY</div>
					<h2>Key Takeaways</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>01</span>
							<p>An AP is uniquely determined if you know the first term <strong>a</strong> and common difference <strong>d</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>02</span>
							<p>Common difference formula: <strong>d = a₂ - a₁ = a₃ - a₂ = ... = a<sub>k+1</sub> - a<sub>k</sub></strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>03</span>
							<p><strong>Finite AP</strong> has a last term; <strong>Infinite AP</strong> continues indefinitely.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- LESSON NAVIGATION -->
					<div class="lesson-navigation">
						<a href="/arithmetic-progressions" class="previous-lesson">
							<span>←</span>
							<div>
								<small>OVERVIEW</small>
								<strong>Chapter Overview</strong>
							</div>
						</a>

						<a href="/arithmetic-progressions/nth-term" class="next-lesson">
							<div>
								<small>NEXT LESSON</small>
								<strong>nth Term of an AP</strong>
							</div>
							<span>→</span>
						</a>
					</div>
				</article>

				<!-- SIDEBAR -->
				<aside class="lesson-sidebar">
					<div class="sidebar-card">
						<div class="sidebar-title">ARITHMETIC PROGRESSIONS</div>
						<div class="progress-text">Lesson 01 of 04</div>
						<div class="progress-bar">
							<div style="width: 25%;"></div>
						</div>

						<div class="sidebar-lessons">
							<a href="/arithmetic-progressions/introduction" class="sidebar-lesson active">
								<span>01</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Introduction to AP</strong>
									<small>First term (a) & difference (d)</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/arithmetic-progressions/nth-term" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>02</span>
								<div>
									<strong>nth Term of an AP</strong>
									<small>Formula aₙ = a + (n-1)d</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/arithmetic-progressions/sum-of-n-terms" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>03</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Sum of First n Terms</strong>
									<small>Formula Sₙ = n/2[2a+(n-1)d]</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/arithmetic-progressions/pyqs" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>04</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Previous Year PYQs</strong>
									<small>CBSE 2020-2024 practice set</small>
								</div>
							</a>
						</div>
					</div>
				</aside>
			</section>
		</div>
	</main>

	<style>
